\ The same raise as tail_boundary_compiled_caller.1z, pinned eager. `boom` carries no stack effect,
\ so eager does not compile it and `go` is the one word that does. `go` reaches `when` through its
\ interpreter fallback boundary. That boundary pushes and pends a frame whether or not the call
\ was in tail position, so this chain carries a `when` row the interpreted chain does not. The
\ interpreted chain is the target.
\
\ eager_tail_boundary_compiled_both.1z declares `boom`'s effect, which compiles the callee too.

boom: [ f "kaboom" EUserThrown make-error throw ] ;
go: ( ? -- ) [ [ boom ] when ] ;

[ t go ] [ inspect print-line ] recover
